      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "and whose sovereignty in heaven is not permanent. प्रतिनियत",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "&c.—एकं केवलमेव फळमेकफलं कर्मण एकफलं कर्मैकफलंः प्रतिनियतं व्यव-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "स्थितं predetermind, fixed कर्मैकफलं ददाति इति, Even Vidhi has no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "arbitrary power to dispense fruits. It is entirely guided by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "men’s actions in the distribution thereof. The poet here distin-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "guishes betweed Vidhi and Karman.—कर्मभ्यः—Every action",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "must bear its fruit, good or bad. Cf. ‘न हि कर्माणि क्षीयन्ते ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Mahábhárata, and the well known Smrti ‘नाभुक्तं क्षीयते कर्म ।’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "न येभ्यः प्रभवति—The dat. by ‘नमःस्वस्तिस्वाहास्वधालंवषड्योगाच्च’ । Pán.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "II. 3 16. Here न प्रभवति is equivalent to नालम् । The gen. may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "also be used with words like प्रभु &c.; ‘प्रभ्वादियोगे षष्ठ्यपि साधुः ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "तेन प्रभुर्बुभूषुर्भुवनत्रयस्येति सिद्धम् । Sid. Kau. The Fig. here is सार",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "which is defined as उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षो भवेत्सारः परावधिः । K. P. X.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "S'ara or climax is that in which excellence rising successively",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "ultimately reaches its culminating point.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 100. कुलालवत्—Like a potter. Here the aff. वत् refers to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "क्रिया viz. the work of forming things which Brahmà has to do",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "like a potter fashioning his clay-things. ब्रह्माण्डभाण्डोदरे—in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "cavity of the immense vessel of the primordial egg, (bursting",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "which Brahmâ came out and out of which the universe sprang);",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "See Manu. I. 11—13 and Mat. P. II. 24. et. seq. उदरे—because",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the two shelves of the egg form the extreme boundaries of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "universe within which every existing thing is situated. नियमित-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "restrained, chained down as it were. विष्णुः—The name is thus",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "popularly derived—यस्माद्विश्वमिदं सर्वं तस्य शक्त्या महात्मनः । तस्मादेवो-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "च्यते विष्णुर्विशधातोः प्रवेशनात् ॥ दशावतार०—two consructions are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "possible:—(1) गहन may be taken as meaning a forest ( दशावतारा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "एव गहनं ) and महासंकटे as a Bah. comp. meaning ‘beset with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "great difficulty.’ (2) The other way is to take गहन as an adj.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "qualifying महासंकटे ( a noun ) meaning ‘the great difficulty.’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "The latter way is preferable. Vishnu was cursed by Dur-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "vàsas to undergo the penalty of being born on the earth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "ten times. The ten incarnations are given in the follow-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "ing couplet——मत्स्यः कूर्मो वराहश्च नरसिंहोथ वामनः । रामो",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "रामश्च कृष्णश्च बुद्धः कल्की च ते दश ॥ रुद्रः—रोदयत्यसुरान् इति fr.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
